      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# MARKDKBERRY.com\n\n*This is a straight upscaler to fix images. It doesnt use the VL to make a prompt from the original image*\n\n- 2mp to test only takes a few mins on 8 steps with a turbo lora. \n- 3mp took 144 seconds for 16:9\n- 4mp took 200 seconds for 16:9\n\n\n## PROMPTS\n\n`upscale <image 1> to make it high detail, realistic. Maintain the likeness of the character as much as possible`\n\n`in image 1 create a full length photograph of the woman in image 2 wearing a blue silk nightgown, barefoot, looking directly at the camera with a neutral expression. no strong shadows. white background. use image 3 and image 4 to define the face.`\n\n`remove the man and horse from the image and replace it with the same man and horse but galloping fast across the same background scene`\n\n`remove the woman from image 1 and replace her with the woman from image 2 looking through binoculars at the camera.`\n\n`Replace the woman in image 1 with the woman from image 2. She is looking through a pair of binoculars, holding them up to her eyes with both hands. Keep her face, hair, clothing and skin tone consistent with image 2. Replace the man reading a book inside the tent in image 1 with the man from image 3, lying in the same position and looking at a book. Keep his face, hair, build and clothing consistent with image 3. Preserve the rest of image 1 exactly as it is: the background, tent, lighting, shadows, color grading, camera angle and composition. Match the lighting and scale of both new people to the scene so they blend in naturally.` \n   - (this also had some negatives: `blurry, distorted face, extra limbs, deformed hands, mismatched lighting, changed background, duplicate people, low quality, artifacts`)"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# MARKDKBERRY.com\n\n*This is a straight upscaler to fix images. It doesnt use the VL to make a prompt from the original image*\n\n- 2mp to test only takes a few mins on 8 steps with a turbo lora. \n- 3mp took 144 seconds for 16:9\n- 4mp took 200 seconds for 16:9\n\n\n## PROMPTS\n\n`upscale <image 1> to make it high detail, realistic. Maintain the likeness of the character as much as possible`\n\n`in image 1 create a full length photograph of the woman in image 2 wearing a blue silk nightgown, barefoot, looking directly at the camera with a neutral expression. no strong shadows. white background. use image 3 and image 4 to define the face.`\n\n`remove the man and horse from the image and replace it with the same man and horse but galloping fast across the same background scene`\n\n`remove the woman from image 1 and replace her with the woman from image 2 looking through binoculars at the camera.`\n\n`Replace the woman in image 1 with the woman from image 2. She is looking through a pair of binoculars, holding them up to her eyes with both hands. Keep her face, hair, clothing and skin tone consistent with image 2. Replace the man reading a book inside the tent in image 1 with the man from image 3, lying in the same position and looking at a book. Keep his face, hair, build and clothing consistent with image 3. Preserve the rest of image 1 exactly as it is: the background, tent, lighting, shadows, color grading, camera angle and composition. Match the lighting and scale of both new people to the scene so they blend in naturally.` \n   - (this also had some negatives: `blurry, distorted face, extra limbs, deformed hands, mismatched lighting, changed background, duplicate people, low quality, artifacts`)"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
